<title>FINLAND: FINNISH 2001 BOND YIELDS 5.05 PCT AT AUCTION.</title>
<headline>FINNISH 2001 BOND YIELDS 5.05 PCT AT AUCTION.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following issue of the</p>
<p>S1/94 bond was announced by the State Treasury Office:</p>
<p> ISSUER:				 Republic of Finland</p>
<p> MATURITY:			     15-05-2001</p>
<p> COUPON:				 10.00 PCT</p>
<p> AUCTION YIELD:			5.05 PCT</p>
<p> AUCTION PRICE:			120.90*</p>
<p> AUCTION AMOUNT			FIM 1,714 MLN</p>
<p> BID AMOUNT:			   FIM 6,315 MLN</p>
<p> PAYMENT FREQUENCY:		  YEARLY</p>
<p>NOTES:</p>
<p>*60 percent of bids accepted at 120.90</p>
<p>After this auction, the outstanding amount is 27,147 million</p>
<p>markka.</p>
<p>The previous auction of the bond raised 1,260 million markka</p>
<p>at a price of 118.75 and a yield of 5.59 percent.</p>
<p>-- Helsinki newsroom +358-0-6805 0245</p>
</text>
